# Cloudflare's Pages-style static-asset header convention (also honored by
# Workers [assets]) -- see https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# Both files need Access-Control-Allow-Origin because both are fetched as
# ES modules, which -- unlike a plain classic <script src> -- are always
# CORS-gated regardless of same-/cross-origin:
# - chirp-core.js: the Canary widget package (canary-widget/chirp.js)
#   loads it via a cross-origin dynamic import() at runtime.
# - chirp-widget.js: the generic embed's own <script type="module"
#   src="https://your-worker.../chirp-widget.js"> tag is *always*
#   cross-origin in real usage -- it's dropped onto a third-party site's
#   own page, pointed at the operator's Worker origin.
# Both are public, non-sensitive static JS (no secrets, no per-user data),
# so a wildcard is fine.
/chirp-core.js
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
/chirp-widget.js
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
